WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:05.319
Varys: Aegon landed at the mouth of the Blackwater
River and raised a primitive Aegonfort in

00:00:05.319 --> 00:00:10.190
the disputed lands between Harren's and Argilac's
kingdom so that neither could decide whose

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:12.019
problem he was.

00:00:12.019 --> 00:00:17.850
Adopting the customs of the Seven Kingdoms,
Aegon unfurled his own banner with a red three-headed

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:21.140
dragon breathing fire upon a black field.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:27.070
Visenya crowned him with a ruby-studded circlet
of Valyrian steel while Rhaenys hailed him

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:31.690
as the first high king the continent had seen
since the Dawn Age.

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:36.890
As his lords and the gathered locals cheered
him, Aegon named his loyal friends to a small

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:43.120
council led by Orys Baratheon, whom he called
"my strong right hand."

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:47.760
The title stuck, and he became the first Hand
of the King.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:54.039
But for now, Aegon's kingdom contained only
a rocky island and a handful of fields.

00:00:54.039 --> 00:00:59.110
The other kings had large armies, ships, castles,
and thousands of years of rule.

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:01.559
But Aegon had dragons.

00:01:01.559 --> 00:01:06.530
He had chosen for the words of his house,
"Fire and Blood."

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:11.290
Before he was done, the rivers, fields, and
skies would turn red.

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:16.670
Viserys Targaryen: Soon after his coronation,
Aegon returned to the mouth of the Blackwater

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:20.800
River, where he had first set foot on Westeros.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:25.460
A small town had since sprouted around his
primitive fort.

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:46.430
To honor their new master, the locals dubbed
it "King's Landing," though it looked more

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:53.409
fit for a hedge knight, with wooden palisades,
muddy streets, and piles of mangled swords

00:01:53.409 --> 00:01:56.229
carted in from every corner of the conquest.

00:01:56.229 --> 00:02:03.270
But when Aegon made it his court, wood became
stone, black mud was buried beneath a Red

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:09.619
Keep, and the collected swords of Aegon's
foes were blasted by dragon fire and became

00:02:09.619 --> 00:02:16.140
a seat fit for the Conqueror and the greatest
dynasty this world has ever known.

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:17.360
House Targaryen.

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:22.950
Varys: King's Landing is both a city and a
curse.

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:26.430
Aegon the Conqueror was the first king to
land there.

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:30.360
His first conquest, a tiny village at the
mouth of the Blackwater River, where he raised

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:31.360
a wooden fort.

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:36.750
When it became clear that Aegon would earn
his title, people flocked to the fort and

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:39.840
renamed it "King's Landing" in his honor.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:45.099
The ploy succeeded, and Aegon chose King's
Landing for his capital over older and more

00:02:45.099 --> 00:02:50.670
beautiful cities like Oldtown and anywhere
else.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:56.590
The currying of royal favor thus became the
foundation of the city, and blood its bricks.

00:02:56.590 --> 00:03:01.980
Maegor the Cruel, Aegon's son, completed the
city's famous Red Keep to hold the trappings

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:07.360
of power: the royal family, the Kingsguard,
and the Iron Throne.

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:13.230
To maintain the new castle's secrets, Maegor
murdered all its masons and craftsmen at a

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:19.430
feast, which he catered with the new castle
servants, who soon found all its secrets for

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:20.430
himself.

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:24.560
When the Faith Militant challenged his rule,
Maegor razed their Sept of Remembrance to

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:29.070
the ground with them inside at prayer and
erected the Dragonpit on the ashes.

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:34.590
Petyr Baelish: Prince Maegor, a warrior who
was proud and arrogant.

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:40.420
Maegor agreed to marry the High Septon's niece
to unite the Faith and the Crown, but then

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:47.010
secretly wed a second wife in a Valyrian ceremony
artfully combining bigamy and heresy.

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:51.260
When word of it got out, the King was forced
to exile Maegor and choose a septon as his

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:52.819
new Hand.

00:03:52.819 --> 00:03:54.700
But the damage had been done.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:59.530
The King had trusted in family, and his brother
had set off a rebellion that would claim his

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:01.290
rule and his life.

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:06.890
The High Sparrow:When Aegon's heir wed his
daughter to his son, the Faith could brook

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:09.599
such abomination no longer.

00:04:09.599 --> 00:04:13.420
The High Septon led the denunciation of the
Targaryens.

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:18.239
And all over Westeros, the Faith Militant
took up their swords against the dynasty and

00:04:18.239 --> 00:04:20.079
its supporters.

00:04:20.079 --> 00:04:25.169
The Faith Militant set upon and punished the
septon who had performed the ceremony.

00:04:25.169 --> 00:04:31.630
A few of the Faith Militant's more militant
members even scaled the walls of the castle

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:37.419
and would have slain the king and his family,
had a knight of the Kingsguard not intervened.

00:04:37.419 --> 00:04:43.810
Frightened, the king fled to Dragonstone,
where he soon died of cramps.

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:48.810
And so ascended the king's younger brother,
Maegor the Cruel.

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:54.449
His first act was to challenge the Faith Militant
to kill him if they believed his rule to be

00:04:54.449 --> 00:04:55.780
ungodly.

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:59.780
To the order's eternal credit, they accepted.

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:07.870
Ser Damon Morrigen proposed a "trial by seven,"
Ser Damon and six of the Faith Militant against

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:10.730
the king and his six champions.

00:05:10.730 --> 00:05:17.050
It was a contest in which the kingdom itself
was at stake, and the accounts and tales are

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.050
many.

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:25.300
But at the end of it, Maegor alone lived,
proving that the throne was rightfully his.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:31.259
He mounted the black dragon, Balerion, and
burned down the sept in King's Landing while

00:05:31.259 --> 00:05:34.910
the Faith Militant were inside at morning
prayers.

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:41.400
The screams of the burning and dying men were
said to echo throughout the city.

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:46.520
Though Maegor had won the trial by seven,
he demanded the complete destruction of the

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:50.030
Faith Militant and the Faith itself, if necessary.

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:53.710
He made war upon the order wherever he found
it.

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:59.940
Yet the Faith Militant would not surrender,
raising armies of their own and turning Maegor's

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:01.930
own lords against him.

00:06:01.930 --> 00:06:08.230
The Father's justice may not always be swift,
but it is certain.

00:06:08.230 --> 00:06:12.300
One morning, Maegor was found dead on the
Iron Throne.

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:13.960
No one knows how.

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:17.120
Maegor's cruelty died with him.

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:24.000
His successor saw the wisdom of a united crown
and faith, and his Hand reached an accord

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.710
with the High Septon.

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:31.819
As long as the Iron Throne defended the Faith,
the Faith would put aside its own swords and

00:06:31.819 --> 00:06:34.940
its condemnation of the Targaryens.

00:06:34.940 --> 00:06:54.500
Viserys Targaryen:The Dance began, as 

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:57.560
many dances do, with an old man and a young
girl.

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:02.160
The queen had failed to produce a son for
her king, so he anointed his daughter, the

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:03.840
Princess Rhaenyra, as his heir.

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:09.070
But years later, the king remarried, and his
new wife, Queen Alicent of House Hightower,

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:10.630
gave him a son.

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:13.870
Feeble and foolish, the old king refused to
change the succession.

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:18.940
He didn't even see how his court had split
into two rival camps of Blacks and Greens,

00:07:18.940 --> 00:07:26.020
after the dresses that the princess and the
queen had worn to some tourney.

00:07:26.020 --> 00:07:30.441
One night, a servant found the old king had
died in his sleep and ran to inform Queen

00:07:30.441 --> 00:07:32.300
Alicent.

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:36.330
Protocol dictated that the bells would be
rung and a raven sent to Dragonstone to summon

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:39.589
the heir, Princess Rhaenyra, for her coronation.

00:07:39.589 --> 00:07:42.050
But Alicent had other plans.

00:07:42.050 --> 00:07:46.210
None were more surprised to hear of Prince
Aegon's succession than Prince Aegon himself.

00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:51.229
At first, the fool rejected the crown, but
his mother pointed out that his sister Rhaenyra

00:07:51.229 --> 00:07:54.590
would return such loyalty by taking his head.

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:57.830
As the old king's trueborn son, he'd always
be a threat.

00:07:57.830 --> 00:07:59.060
Aegon relented.

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:03.030
He was crowned in the Dragonpit, and his wife
and sister Helaena became queen.

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:07.319
His brother Aemond flew off to win over the
few great lords whose support Aegon didn't

00:08:07.319 --> 00:08:08.319
already have.

00:08:08.319 --> 00:08:13.600
The banner of the gold dragon flew over King's
Landing and the Red Keep as Aegon, Second

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:16.740
of His Name, ascended the Iron Throne.

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:17.990
He would not sit it long.

00:08:17.990 --> 00:08:23.990
Robert Baratheon: One day King's Landing looked
up and saw two dragons circling their foul

00:08:23.990 --> 00:08:24.990
city.

00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:29.600
Daemon and Rhaenyra had come for her throne,
for the city was defenseless.

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:37.630
Aemond had taken the king's army from the
city, and worse, he'd taken his dragon Vhagar.

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:43.030
Seeing that resistance was hopeless, the small
council surrendered the city, the Queen Mother

00:08:43.030 --> 00:08:46.960
Alicent, and the broken Queen Helaena.

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:48.970
But not King Aegon.

00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:55.050
Somehow, despite his wounds and delirium,
he had vanished from the city.

00:08:55.050 --> 00:09:00.990
And so Queen Rhaenyra climbed the steps and
seated herself of the Iron Throne.

00:09:00.990 --> 00:09:07.050
Legend has it that as she left that hall later,
blood trickled down her legs and hands, proving

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:10.019
the Iron Throne had spurned her.

00:09:10.019 --> 00:09:11.450
Nonsense!

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:14.300
It's a chair made of steel blades.

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:19.610
Rhaenyra had wanted it all her life and had
sacrificed two sons for it.

00:09:19.610 --> 00:09:22.540
She likely gripped the damn thing too tight.

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:27.470
Shireen Baratheon: When Rhaenyra's last son
wed Aegon's only daughter, the Dance of Dragons

00:09:27.470 --> 00:09:28.470
officially ended.

00:09:28.470 --> 00:09:30.200
Ash and burned men.

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:34.660
All that was left of the Riverlands.

00:09:34.660 --> 00:09:37.890
Two scared children spouting oaths they didn't
understand.

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:42.840
All that was left of the mighty House Targaryen.

00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:47.230
Ancient skulls and hatchlings that grew no
bigger than cats.

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:49.010
All that was left of the dragons.

00:09:49.010 --> 00:09:54.431
The High Sparrow: To steward his monument
to vanity, Baelor summoned the High Septon

00:09:54.431 --> 00:10:00.670
of the Faith from his ancient seat in Oldtown
and gifted him with ornate robes and a crown

00:10:00.670 --> 00:10:02.839
of crystal and gold.

00:10:02.839 --> 00:10:10.700
And like a fool, the High Septon put on his
lord's motley and danced at his lord's table,

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:17.090
and with each passing year, the High Septons
fell ever lower.

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:23.290
How can the flock be kept safe from wolves
when the shepherd sleeps in their den?

00:10:23.290 --> 00:10:29.740
Baelor himself appointed a simple-minded stonemason,
believing him the Smith reborn.

00:10:29.740 --> 00:10:36.200
And when he died, Baelor replaced him with
an eight-year-old boy whom Baelor had seen

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:41.070
speaking with doves that answered with the
voices of the Seven.

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:46.470
Still, the common people revere Baelor as
the Blessed.

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:52.670
They tell of how he forced a high lord to
wash a beggar's feet, fasted to tame his unnatural

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:58.470
lusts and walked the Boneway himself to make
peace with Dorne.

00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:03.529
Many septons and septas even claim that Baelor
rescued his cousin, the Dragonknight, from

00:11:03.529 --> 00:11:10.570
a snake pit because no viper would strike
a man so pure and holy.

00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:12.279
A lie!

00:11:12.279 --> 00:11:19.000
Baelor was bitten a dozen times and was bedridden
for half a year, and yet he didn't die.

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:24.840
Petyr Baelish: When the last dragon died,
it was only a matter of time before the Targaryens

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:25.840
followed.

00:11:25.840 --> 00:11:29.029
Varys: By "only," you mean another century?

00:11:29.029 --> 00:11:34.740
Baelish: Which they wasted trying to replace
their lost advantage: incinerating their own

00:11:34.740 --> 00:11:40.970
palaces to hatch dragon eggs, drinking wildfire
to become dragons, and, let's not forget the

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:47.029
Mad King's favorite, burning men alive so
he could pretend to be a dragon.

00:11:47.029 --> 00:11:48.889
Jaime Lannister: Kingslayer.

00:11:48.889 --> 00:11:54.940
A word every man and woman in Westeros spits
at me, though many can't name the king I slayed.

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:56.480
I understand.

00:11:56.480 --> 00:12:00.910
To them, I'm a symbol of everything they'll
never have and a warning that'll never apply.

00:12:00.910 --> 00:12:04.740
So they can loathe me from the safety of their
small lives.

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:08.070
But when a dog goes mad, we put it down.

00:12:08.070 --> 00:12:09.329
Why not a king?

00:12:09.329 --> 00:12:14.500
I served at the king's pleasure as he burned
Rickard Stark alive and strangled his son,

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:16.260
inciting the rebellion.

00:12:16.260 --> 00:12:21.570
I defended the king's honor against courtiers
as his generals lost battle after battle with

00:12:21.570 --> 00:12:22.570
Robert.

00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:27.579
I kept the king's secrets when his pyromancers
hid caches of wildfire beneath King's Landing.

00:12:27.579 --> 00:12:33.420
I gave the king counsel when my father's army
was at the city gate, and Grand Maester Pycelle

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:36.639
lied that my father had come to save him.

00:12:36.639 --> 00:12:39.800
Many forget that I also tried to defend the
king from harm.

00:12:39.800 --> 00:12:43.520
When the Lannister soldiers poured through
the gates, it fell to me to hold the Red Keep

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:45.649
as the only Kingsguard in the city.

00:12:45.649 --> 00:12:49.260
I knew we were lost and sent to Aerys, asking
his leave to make terms.

00:12:49.260 --> 00:12:52.070
My man came back with the royal command.

00:12:52.070 --> 00:12:57.149
"Bring me your father's head if you are no
traitor."

00:12:57.149 --> 00:12:58.839
Aerys would have no yielding.

00:12:58.839 --> 00:13:01.720
His pyromancer was with him, my messenger
said.

00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:04.120
I knew what that meant.

00:13:04.120 --> 00:13:08.459
Aerys Targaryen was alone in his throne room
when I found him, picking at his scabbed and

00:13:08.459 --> 00:13:09.590
bleeding hands.

00:13:09.590 --> 00:13:13.170
The fool was always cutting himself on the
Iron Throne.

00:13:13.170 --> 00:13:14.170
"Burn them!

00:13:14.170 --> 00:13:16.150
Burn them!" he kept muttering.

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:22.070
Aerys had decided to let Robert be king, after
all, over the charred bones and ashes of King's

00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:23.070
Landing.

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:27.139
He must have thought his pyromancer was near
enough to obey him, but I'd killed him a few

00:13:27.139 --> 00:13:28.940
minutes before in the courtyard.

00:13:28.940 --> 00:13:33.740
As I approached the throne, sanity flashed
behind the King's eyes for a moment, just

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:35.850
long enough to read the look in mine.

00:13:35.850 --> 00:13:39.430
His eyes grew huge, and the royal mouth drooped
open in shock.

00:13:39.430 --> 00:13:41.300
He turned and ran.

00:13:41.300 --> 00:13:48.820
A single thrust was all it took to end the
greatest dynasty the world had ever seen.

00:13:48.820 --> 00:13:54.190
Beneath the empty eyes of the dead dragons
on the walls, the last dragon king squealed

00:13:54.190 --> 00:13:56.490
like a pig and shat himself.

00:13:56.490 --> 00:13:59.600
So easy, I thought.

00:13:59.600 --> 00:14:01.759
A king should die harder than this.

